Date: Wed, 15 Sep 93 13:38:15 PDT  
From: "Randall M. Clague" <rclague@netcom.com>
Subject: depression

<<five days straight?>>

Well, a little bent, after 50+ hours...but you pick up your second wind on
the morning of the third day.  You function (poorly) in a mental twilight
zone - but you function.  A few minutes of catnaps as opportunity allows
makes a big difference - if you can catch 2-3 minutes of sleep several times
a shift, that's 3 hours a day.

Two points are interesting about extended sleep deprivation.  1) You have to
be in good physical shape.  If you aren't, your body gives up and down you
go, but not before suffering headaches, sore feet, mood swings, etc.  2) You
start dreaming within seconds of drifting off.  What I find is that the
normal wandering thoughts we all have, just wander farther as we drift off.
In a minute or two, they wander far enough that you know you're dreaming, so
you wake up and check out the situation.  If everything's OK (or at a party,
if nothing interesting is going on), you drift off again.

